-- title:
--   Nonvanishing discriminant of the full-kernel quotient at every level
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. The assertion is the predicate `FullKernelDiscAt N`, namely: for every algebraically closed field $L$ (in the base universe, with decidable equality) in which $2 \neq 0$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $L$ that is elliptic, and every point $Q$ of the affine curve $W$ whose additive order `addOrderOf Q` equals $N$, the Weierstrass curve `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` has nonzero discriminant, $\Delta \neq 0$. Here `W.fullKernelQuotient Q N` is the curve `W.veluQuotientOfSums s t` built from the two Vélu sums taken over the finite set `W.oddOrderSummingSet Q (N - 1)`: the first argument is $s = \sum_P \mathrm{veluGx}(P_1, P_2)$ and the second is $t = \sum_P \bigl(P_1 \cdot \mathrm{veluGx}(P_1,P_2) - P_2 \cdot \mathrm{veluGy}(P_1,P_2)\bigr)$, the sums running over the coordinate pairs $P$ of that set. Thus the conclusion is that for every level $N$, even as well as odd, the Vélu-type quotient of $W$ by the cyclic group generated by a point of exact order $N$ is again nondegenerate.
--
--   This is the nondegeneracy statement for the quotient of an elliptic curve by a cyclic subgroup of order $N$ computed by Vélu's formulae: the quotient curve is again elliptic, which is what makes statements about its $j$-invariant meaningful. It is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_elliptic_cycSub_orbitMap), in the construction of elliptic curves with prescribed cyclic subgroup data on the modular curve side.
